            "result_text": "I'll help you set up a git server with automatic deployment to a webserver. This involves creating a bare git repository with a post-receive hook that deploys to the web directory.\n\nHere's what you need to do on the server:\n\n**1. Create the bare git repository:**\n```bash\nsudo mkdir -p /git/server\ncd /git/server\ngit init --bare\n```\n\n**2. Create a post-receive hook** that deploys changes to the webserver:\n```bash\nsudo tee /git/server/hooks/post-receive > /dev/null <<'EOF'\n#!/bin/bash\n\nWORK_DIR=\"/tmp/git-deploy\"\nWEB_DIR=\"/var/www/html\"\n\n# Clone/update working copy\nif [ ! -d \"$WORK_DIR\" ]; then\n    git clone /git/server \"$WORK_DIR\"\nelse\n    cd \"$WORK_DIR\"\n    git pull\nfi\n\n# Copy files to webserver\ncp -r \"$WORK_DIR\"/* \"$WEB_DIR\"/ 2>/dev/null || true\n\necho \"Deployed to $WEB_DIR\"\nEOF\n\nsudo chmod +x /git/server/hooks/post-receive\nsudo chown git:git -R /git/server  # or whatever user runs git\n```\n\n**3. Set up the webserver on port 8080:**\n\n**Option A: Using Python (simplest)**\n```bash\nsudo tee /etc/systemd/system/webserver.service > /dev/null <<'EOF'\n[Unit]\nDescription=Simple Web Server on Port 8080\nAfter=network.target\n\n[Service]\nType=simple\nWorkingDirectory=/var/www/html\nExecStart=/usr/bin/python3 -m http.server 8080\nRestart=on-failure\nUser=www-data\n\n[Install]\nWantedBy=multi-user.target\nEOF\n\nsudo mkdir -p /var/www/html\nsudo systemctl daemon-reload\nsudo systemctl enable webserver\nsudo systemctl start webserver\n```\n\n**Option B: Using nginx**\n```bash\nsudo apt-get install nginx\n\nsudo tee /etc/nginx/sites-available/default > /dev/null <<'EOF'\nserver {\n    listen 8080;\n    server_name _;\n    root /var/www/html;\n    index index.html;\n}\nEOF\n\nsudo systemctl restart nginx\n```\n\n**4. Fix permissions** so the git hook can write to the web directory:\n```bash\nsudo mkdir -p /var/www/html\nsudo chown www-data:www-data /var/www/html\nsudo chmod 755 /var/www/html\n```\n\nThen from your local machine:\n```bash\ngit clone user@server:/git/server\ncd server\necho \"hello world\" > hello.html\ngit add hello"
